// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 21-standard-library-semantics
// facility: rule.stdlib.x509 [Verify-Chain] (D-0160); conf.x509-name-constraints-and-paths
// kind: positive
// expect: ok
//
// `verify_chain`'s name constraints, its search over candidate issuers and
// the constraints of an anchor and of an issuer's usage, on certificates
// made with Python's `cryptography` (valid 2025 to 2045, checked at
// 2030-01-01). An intermediate whose critical name constraints permit
// `good.test` and 10.0.0.0/8 and exclude `bad.good.test`: names inside are
// accepted, `evil.example`, `bad.good.test`, a wildcard verified for the
// excluded host, and an address outside are `NotAuthority`; one whose constraint is a
// directoryName is `UnhandledCritical`. An expired and a renewed
// intermediate of the same name and key, in either order: the renewed one
// is found. A root with path length 0: a leaf under it directly verifies,
// one under an intermediate is `NotAuthority`. An intermediate whose
// extended key usage is clientAuth only: `WrongUsage`.

